// Khong gian lam viec Go — chin module trong mot kho.
//
// VI SAO CO TEP NAY: moi don vi trien khai la mot module rieng, nhung trong luc phat trien
// thi mot sua doi o `core/` phai thay duoc ngay o ca tam dich vu. Khong co go.work, moi lan
// dung `core` la mot vong phat hanh phien ban roi tam lan `go get` — chi phi phoi hop du lon
// de nguoi ta bat dau tranh sua `core`, va ma dung chung khong ai dam sua la ma se bi chep.
//
// go.work CHI danh cho may tram va may chu build. No KHONG di vao anh Docker: moi Dockerfile
// chep dung `core/` + module cua dich vu va dua vao `replace` trong go.mod cua dich vu ay —
// tuc anh chung minh duoc dich vu build duoc ma khong can ca kho.

go 1.26.0

// Why the toolchain is pinned to an exact patch: govulncheck judges the standard library by
// the toolchain running it, and go1.26.2 carried ~107 called stdlib findings (crypto/tls,
// crypto/x509, net, encoding/xml GO-2026-6088 ...) fixed only by go1.26.6. With
// GOTOOLCHAIN=auto an older local go downloads this one instead of building with holes.
// The same line sits in every go.mod and GO_VERSION in every service-*/Dockerfile — raise
// all of them together, never one.
toolchain go1.26.6

use (
	./core
	./service-comms
	./service-documents
	./service-finance
	./service-identity
	./service-petitions
	./service-platform
	./service-reporting
	./tools
)
